    "message": "fix(upgrade): sweep orphans on every upgrade, not only when one is available\n\nBoth sweep calls sit behind \"something needs updating\" — one inside the CLI\nbranch, one inside the compass branch, the latter existing precisely as the\nfallback for the former. #376 then tightened the compass gate to skip\nrelease-bundled compasses, which is every install from v0.9.3 on. So a user on\nthe latest CLI with a release compass now runs `ix upgrade` and reclaims\nnothing, and an interrupted swap is never restored.\n\nThat matters most for this PR: the archives it teaches the sweep about are\nmulti-MB, and the stated reason for sweeping them is that leaving os.tmpdir()\nalso left the OS's own cleanup. A sweep that only runs when an update happens\nto be available does not deliver that.\n\nOne readdir of ~/.ix when there is nothing to do. The calls inside\nprepareDownloadDir stay — that is where the sweep-before-scratch ordering is\nenforced — and simply find nothing.\n\n753 green, lint clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
